  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1255 AM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nA ridge of high pressure to the south will allow for ample hot and \nhumid conditions today to start off the week as southerly \nreturn flow continues to keep dewpoints well in the 70s. Daily \nhigh temperatures in the low to mid 90s will translate to heat\nindex values of 103 to 109 degrees. Have extended the Heat \nAdvisory into Thursday, while Perry County, IL has been upgraded\nto an Extreme Heat Warning for heat index values of 107 to 113 \ndegrees. \n\nWhile the heat is the main headline, a series of shortwaves begin to \nround the ridge as early as Tuesday night, and continue through the \nend of the week. The ECMWF/NAM are more aggressive compared to the \nGFS/CMC in bringing rain chances associated with a MCS in\nsooner. Meanwhile, the consensus on the NBM remains drier, \nsupporting Wednesday evening and Thursday evening having the \ngreatest risk with a 40-50%. A few stronger storms will be \npossible with ML guidance remaining consistent in showing some \nlow severe probabilities. However, the better synoptic setup to \nsupport severe weather remains more north and east at this time.\nLocally heavy rainfall will be possible where storms develop \nwith upwards a half to one inch. \n\nBy Thursday night into Friday, a cold front eventually washes out \nand becomes stationary across the FA, keeping lingering rain \nchances around 20% in the forecast into next weekend. While \nsome minor relief from the heat is expected, heat index values \nare still progged to remain elevated near 100 degrees.",
